From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:09:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 130/342] meson_vdec: H.264; edge-triggered interrupts; the
 canvas module

H.264 with the GXBB firmware (its 20 KB extension in a buffer of its own):
the firmware asks for frames once it has read the SPS (command 1), which a
thread of the session answers with the reference count + 5 frames (at most
24), one area each, and the motion vector buffer; frames come up to six a
report with their stream offsets (WRITE gives the offsets of the data), two
hand-back slots. The end of the stream is a 16x16 IDR picture, whose own
frame request is left unanswered. Facts: the port's docs/m26-vdec-h264-facts.md.

The interrupts are edges as the device tree says; GET_FRAME waits no longer
than its timeout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
